ed in IL, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $1.1bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 9.8% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 73.7%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($173.4m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818201/000119312526324993/0001193125-26-324993-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-324993"},{"text":"Gross margin of 73.7% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818201/000119312526324993/0001193125-26-324993-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-324993"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $173.4m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818201/000095017025063985/0000950170-25-063985-index.htm","accession":"0000950170-25-063985"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-11.5% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818201/000119312526324993/0001193125-26-324993-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-324993"}],"bear":[{"text":"Insiders disposed of 4.0% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (56,168 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818201/000181820126000040/0001818201-26-000040-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.2% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1818201/000181820126000040/0001818201-26-000040-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 66.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.66,"consecutive":2,"current":0.737,"current_display":"73.7%","threshold_display":"66.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -5.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.05,"consecutive":2,"current":0.098,"current_display":"9.8%","threshold_display":"-5.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":-0.115,"current_display":"-11.5%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.20","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.2,"consecutive":1,"current":0.718,"current_display":"0.72","threshold_display":"1.20","fired":false,"rationale":"Past th